---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import LegalContact from '../components/LegalContact.astro';
import { legalDetails, legalValue } from '../data/legal';
const sections = [
  { id: 'parties', title: 'Parties and scope' },
  { id: 'eligibility', title: 'Eligibility and lawful use' },
  { id: 'enquiries', title: 'Enquiries and contract formation' },
  { id: 'engagements', title: 'Scope, fees and changes' },
  { id: 'responsibilities', title: 'Client responsibilities' },
  { id: 'confidentiality', title: 'Client data and confidentiality' },
  { id: 'intellectual-property', title: 'Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'examples', title: 'Website tools and AI outputs' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', title: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'availability', title: 'Availability and third-party services' },
  { id: 'liability', title: 'Warranties and liability' },
  { id: 'termination', title: 'Suspension and termination' },
  { id: 'disputes', title: 'Indian law and dispute resolution' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes and general provisions' },
  { id: 'notices', title: 'Company details and legal notices' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms governing the QWERTY Labs website, workflow tools and separately agreed client services."
  sections={sections}
  relatedHref="/privacy/"
  relatedLabel="Privacy Policy"
>
  <section id="parties" aria-labelledby="parties-title">
    <h2 id="parties-title">1. Parties and scope</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) state the conditions on which{' '}
      {legalValue('legalEntityName')}, trading as {legalDetails.tradingName}{' '}
      (“QWERTY Labs”, “we”, “us” or “our”), at {legalValue('businessAddress')},
      makes this website, its content and browser-based tools available. “You”
      means the person using them and, where applicable, the organisation that
      person is authorised to represent.
    </p>
    <p>
      Client services require a separate written agreement accepted by both
      parties. That agreement must identify the contracting parties and the
      applicable scope. Its expressly agreed service terms govern the
      engagement; these website Terms do not unilaterally alter it. Mandatory
      law takes precedence over a conflicting contractual provision.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Privacy Policy explains data handling. Reading or using the website
      does not itself provide consent for unrelated processing of personal
      information.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="eligibility" aria-labelledby="eligibility-title">
    <h2 id="eligibility-title">2. Eligibility and lawful use</h2>
    <p>
      A person requesting or entering a service agreement must be at least
      eighteen years old, competent to contract under Indian law and, if acting
      for an organisation, authorised to bind it. Information provided for a
      business discussion must be accurate to the best of that person's
      knowledge. Website access must comply with applicable law and these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="enquiries" aria-labelledby="enquiries-title">
    <h2 id="enquiries-title">3. Enquiries and contract formation</h2>
    <p>
      Contact and Book a Demo forms allow you to describe your requirements and
      request a conversation. An enquiry or its automated confirmation does not
      reserve an appointment, place an order, accept a quotation or create a
      service agreement. A demo time must be agreed separately.
    </p>
    <p>
      Website descriptions are an invitation to discuss requirements. A client
      engagement begins only when authorised representatives accept the relevant
      written agreement, including by a legally valid electronic method where
      agreed. An automated confirmation is not acceptance of an engagement by
      QWERTY Labs.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="engagements" aria-labelledby="engagements-title">
    <h2 id="engagements-title">4. Scope, fees and changes</h2>
    <p>
      Before paid work begins, the service agreement or statement of work must
      specify deliverables, assumptions, client inputs, integrations,
      milestones, acceptance criteria, fees, payment dates, applicable taxes,
      operating charges and any support period. No price, delivery date,
      integration, service level or model release is promised merely by its
      appearance in an illustrative example.
    </p>
    <p>
      Changes to scope, timing or charges require agreement through the
      engagement's change process. Cancellation, refunds, unearned advances and
      work already performed must be addressed in that agreement, subject to
      mandatory law.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="responsibilities" aria-labelledby="responsibilities-title">
    <h2 id="responsibilities-title">5. Client responsibilities</h2>
    <p>
      For an agreed engagement, the client is responsible for supplying the
      information, decisions and access allocated to it in the scope, and for
      having authority to provide that material. Personal information,
      recordings and protected material must be supported by the notices,
      permissions, licences or other lawful basis required for the intended use.
    </p>
    <p>
      The parties must identify who approves actions, reviews outputs and
      administers the relevant systems. A client dependency or change affecting
      delivery must be discussed promptly; any resulting change to price or
      timing requires the agreed contractual process. This allocation does not
      excuse QWERTY Labs from its own legal or contractual obligations.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="confidentiality" aria-labelledby="confidentiality-title">
    <h2 id="confidentiality-title">6. Client data and confidentiality</h2>
    <p>
      Client Data has the meaning given in the Privacy Policy. The client and
      its licensors retain their rights in that material. QWERTY Labs may
      process it only for the agreed engagement and lawful instructions; access
      is restricted to authorised staff who need it for the task.
    </p>
    <p>
      QWERTY Labs does not use Client Data to train or fine-tune its own or
      third-party models or add it to training datasets. Before a contractor,
      hosting provider or model service receives it, the parties must establish
      permitted processing, confidentiality, training restrictions, locations,
      retention and the required authorisation.
    </p>
    <p>
      For an engagement, each party must protect the other's non-public business
      information and use it only for the agreed purpose. Disclosure is limited
      to persons bound by appropriate confidentiality obligations or to the
      extent legally required. Information is excluded only where the recipient
      can demonstrate that it was lawfully public, already lawfully known,
      independently developed or lawfully obtained without a confidentiality
      duty.
    </p>
    <p>
      The project agreement must specify security measures, incident cooperation
      and return or deletion of data. Those terms cannot reduce mandatory
      protection. Confidentiality obligations continue after completion or
      termination. Neither party may use the other's name, logo or confidential
      project information in publicity without written permission.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section
    id="intellectual-property"
    aria-labelledby="intellectual-property-title"
  >
    <h2 id="intellectual-property-title">7. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Website text, design, original figures, software and branding belong to
      QWERTY Labs or the relevant rights holders. You may read, reference and
      download material made available for that purpose for lawful personal or
      internal business use, retaining attribution and notices. Redistribution,
      republication or commercial exploitation requires permission unless a
      stated licence or applicable law permits it. Third-party research and
      materials retain their own rights and licence conditions.
    </p>
    <p>
      You retain your rights in workflows and material you create or import into
      the browser-based designer. Using the tool does not transfer those rights
      to QWERTY Labs. Rights in commissioned deliverables, pre-existing tools,
      source code, model weights and third-party components must be specified in
      the client agreement. No exclusive ownership of model-generated output or
      assignment of rights is implied by a website example.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="examples" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
    <h2 id="examples-title">8. Website tools and AI outputs</h2>
    <p>
      Worked examples, calculations and sample dialogues illustrate proposed
      behaviour. They are not reports of a customer deployment or guaranteed
      performance. Proprietary-model development directions do not represent
      released models or an undertaking to release them on a particular date.
    </p>
    <p>
      The workflow designer is a browser-based planning tool. Its walkthroughs
      evaluate workflow logic using the selected scenario data. Exported JSON
      and diagrams are design documents; they do not deploy automation or
      authorise a real-world transaction. Users must manage local drafts and
      downloaded copies on their own devices.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI outputs can be inaccurate, incomplete or unsuitable for a particular
      decision. A production engagement must establish representative
      evaluation, appropriate review and authorised actions. Website examples
      are not a substitute for that work or for advice from a qualified
      professional where the subject requires it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="acceptable-use" aria-labelledby="acceptable-use-title">
    <h2 id="acceptable-use-title">9. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You must not use the website or sample tools to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Access systems or information without authority, evade access controls,
        introduce malicious code or disrupt services.
      </li>
      <li>
        Infringe intellectual-property, confidentiality or privacy rights, or
        process material you are not entitled to use.
      </li>
      <li>
        Impersonate another person, make fraudulent representations or use an
        example as a false claim of approval or performance.
      </li>
      <li>
        Attempt to connect sample workflows to live systems through an
        unauthorised mechanism.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Security testing that could affect the site or others requires prior
      written authorisation. Ordinary use of the available design and export
      functions remains subject to applicable law.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="availability" aria-labelledby="availability-title">
    <h2 id="availability-title">10. Availability and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      The free website and prototypes may be changed, interrupted or withdrawn
      for maintenance, security, legal or operational reasons. No
      continuous-availability commitment applies to them. A paid engagement's
      service levels and change obligations are determined by its agreement.
    </p>
    <p>
      External links are provided for reference. The linked operator's terms
      apply to its service. Selection of a third-party model, infrastructure or
      integration for client work requires the assessment and agreement
      described in the scope and Privacy Policy; a reference on this website is
      not a guarantee of that provider's availability or suitability.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="liability" aria-labelledby="liability-title">
    <h2 id="liability-title">11. Warranties and liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent Indian law permits, free website content and sample tools
      are provided as available, without a promise that they will meet a
      particular production requirement or be free from every error. We remain
      responsible for express commitments and liabilities that cannot lawfully
      be excluded. Paid services are subject to the warranties, remedies and
      allocation of risk expressly agreed for them.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent legally permitted, neither party is liable under these
      website Terms for indirect or consequential loss, or loss that was not
      reasonably foreseeable from the relevant breach. This does not exclude
      recovery that applicable law requires.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these Terms excludes liability for fraud, wilful misconduct,
      gross negligence, breach of an applicable confidentiality or
      data-protection obligation, or any other liability that cannot lawfully be
      restricted. Statutory consumer rights and remedies remain available where
      the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 applies.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="termination" aria-labelledby="termination-title">
    <h2 id="termination-title">12. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      Website access may be restricted where reasonably necessary to address a
      breach of these Terms, unlawful activity or a security risk. Notice and an
      opportunity to resolve the matter will be given where practicable;
      immediate action may be taken where required for security or law.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ending a client engagement, cure periods, payment for completed work,
      treatment of advances and transition assistance are governed by its
      agreement and applicable law. Ending access does not transfer ownership of
      Client Data or authorise its use for another purpose. Return, deletion and
      lawful retention must follow the agreed data-handling terms.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="disputes" aria-labelledby="disputes-title">
    <h2 id="disputes-title">13. Indian law and dispute resolution</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of India, including the Indian
      Contract Act, 1872 and the Information Technology Act, 2000, as
      applicable. The parties should first attempt to resolve a dispute through
      a written notice describing the issue and the remedy sought. That process
      does not suspend a statutory limitation period or prevent urgent relief.
    </p>
    <p>
      Subject to mandatory law, courts at {legalValue('jurisdictionCity')},{' '}
      {legalValue('jurisdictionState')}, India shall have jurisdiction only to
      the extent those courts otherwise have territorial, subject-matter and
      pecuniary jurisdiction. This provision does not confer jurisdiction on an
      otherwise incompetent court.
    </p>
    <p>
      No website term requires compulsory arbitration or prevents a person from
      approaching a competent consumer commission, regulator or other statutory
      forum where the law permits. Any arbitration arrangement for a client
      engagement requires a separately accepted written agreement.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
    <h2 id="changes-title">14. Changes and general provisions</h2>
    <p>
      Revised website Terms will display their revision and effective dates.
      Changes apply prospectively, with notice and acceptance where required. A
      website update does not amend an existing client agreement; amendments to
      it require the agreed process.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a provision is unenforceable, it will be applied only to the lawful
      extent, and the remaining provisions continue where they can operate
      independently. A failure to enforce a provision on one occasion is not a
      waiver of it. These Terms do not create a partnership, agency or
      employment relationship.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="notices" aria-labelledby="notices-title">
    <h2 id="notices-title">15. Company details and legal notices</h2>
    <p>
      For contractual or website-related legal notices, use the details below or
      follow the notice procedure in an existing client agreement. Privacy
      requests should use the contact route in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>
    <LegalContact />
    <p>
      A legal notice must follow any procedure required by applicable law or an
      existing agreement. An enquiry confirmation does not waive those
      requirements.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
